INT. SLEEPER SHIP CRYO-BAY, DECK TWELVE - NIGHT CYCLE

Rows of frosted pods stretch into blue gloom. Mist curls along the floor. A soft chime counts the hours.

ARCHIVIST NADIA ABERNATHY-OSEI (30s, close-cropped hair, wool cardigan over a ship's jumpsuit) walks the aisle with a tablet. Her assistant, DR. FELIX OYAMA-BRENNAN (40s, thin, tired eyes), trails behind with a thermos.

NADIA
(to the room)
Everyone's temperature is nominal.

FELIX
Do they hear you?

NADIA
No.

FELIX
Then why report?

NADIA
Habit.

She stops at a pod. The frost inside has thinned to a clear oval, and behind it a sleeping face is visible.

NADIA (CONT'D)
(murmuring)
Hello, Pod Four-Eleven.

ONBOARD AI (V.O.)
Pod Four-Eleven is scheduled for revival in four hundred and twelve years.

FELIX
Four hundred and twelve. Time flies.

Felix sips from the thermos. Nadia wipes a smear of frost from the glass. Under her thumb, the sleeper's eyelid flickers.

NADIA (CONT'D)
Felix.

FELIX
Hm?

NADIA
Four-Eleven is dreaming.

FELIX
Everyone dreams.

NADIA
Not in cryo.

ONBOARD AI (V.O.)
Anomaly logged. Please remain calm.

Felix drops the thermos. In the pod, the eyelid opens.
